--
N5008 [expr.new]/24: the new-initializer `{3}' direct-list-initializes the
object; [dcl.init.list]/3.4: node is an aggregate, so its member v is
initialized from 3.  The front end treated the one-element list as a
conversion of 3 to node ("invalid implicit conversion from 'signed int' to
'struct node'") and rejected the unit; typecheck_expr_new now
aggregate-initializes the new object for a one-element list; two elements (`new point{1, 2}') and
`node n{3}' work.  Found while reproducing the shared_ptr group of the
round-163 audit (`p.reset(new node{3})').  Header-free.  Fails on the
round-163 build bin52.
